{#
  The group page's side column, below the search box — who is in this
  group, and what has been photographed in it lately.

  Drawn ONLY from 992px up: show.html.twig hides the block below that
  breakpoint (`d-none d-lg-block`), and components.css places it in the
  second grid track above it. This is a use for width the feed gave back
  when it was capped at 680px, not a section moved to the bottom of a
  phone page — the feed paginates as you scroll (groups.js), so anything
  placed after it there is content nobody reaches.

  Both blocks are teasers: a glance, then the real page underneath. The
  members list and the gallery both already exist as pages of their own,
  and neither is duplicated here — this column shows the first few rows
  of each and links to them.

  Expects: group, side_members, side_members_total, side_photos
  (Controller\GroupController::show()).
#}
<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h6 mb-2">Membres</h2>
        {% if side_members is empty %}
            {% include 'partials/empty_state.html.twig' with {
                message: 'Aucun membre à afficher.',
                compact: true,
            } only %}
        {% else %}
            <ul class="list-unstyled mb-2">
                {% for member in side_members %}
                    <li class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 py-1">
                        {#
                          The shared avatar component (person_avatar(),
                          Core\View\PersonAvatar) keyed on the MEMBER, so
                          it resolves the member's own photo for the year
                          rather than the photo of whichever account is
                          linked to them — a parent's face next to their
                          child's name is exactly the mix-up that function
                          refuses to make.
                        #}
                        {{ person_avatar(member.identity.account_name, { member_id: member.member_id, size: 32 }) }}
                        {#
                          Named through the shared partial, like every
                          other surface of this module with room for
                          markup: the account in front, its memberships
                          for the year in parentheses behind. A flat
                          string here would be this module's one place
                          where the same person reads differently.

                          text-break rather than text-truncate: a flex
                          item will not shrink below its own content
                          without a min-width:0 this project has no
                          utility for, so truncating would overflow the
                          card instead of ellipsizing. A long name wraps.
                        #}
                        <span class="small text-break">
                            {% include '@groups/partials/identity.html.twig' with { identity: member.identity } only %}
                        </span>
                    </li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
            {% if side_members_total > side_members|length %}
                <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-2">
                    et {{ side_members_total - side_members|length }}
                    autre{{ side_members_total - side_members|length > 1 ? 's' : '' }}
                </p>
            {% endif %}
        {% endif %}
        <a class="small text-decoration-none" href="/groups/{{ group.id }}/members">
            Voir tous les membres
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

{#
  No photo yet, no block: an empty three-cell strip in a side column says
  nothing a reader can act on, and the header already carries a permanent
  « Galerie » button for the page itself.
#}
{% if side_photos is not empty %}
    <div class="card">
        <div class="card-body">
            <h2 class="h6 mb-2">Dernières photos</h2>
            {#
              ONE link around the whole strip rather than one per
              thumbnail: six links reading "photo" in a row is six stops
              for a keyboard or a screen reader, all of them going to the
              same place. The photos open in the group's gallery, which is
              where the real viewer (gallery's lightbox) lives — these
              cells carry none of its trigger attributes on purpose, so
              they cannot join the feed's own lightbox set.
            #}
            <a href="/groups/{{ group.id }}/gallery"
               class="groups-side-photo-grid text-decoration-none"
               aria-label="Voir toutes les photos du groupe">
                {% for photo in side_photos %}
                    <img src="/gallery/media/{{ photo.id }}/thumb" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
                {% endfor %}
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endif %}
